From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bump follow-redirects 1.16.1->1.16.2 for CVE-2026-116689

Upstream: https://github.com/follow-redirects/follow-redirects/commit/b0a7751e9cd64cd8eeb6ec67d2f206a9cc88d3f8

From 1.16.0 until 1.16.2, the documented sensitiveHeaders option is
checked with value instanceof Array, so an array created in another
JavaScript realm is replaced with an empty list even though
Array.isArray recognizes it. When a request then follows an
attacker-controlled cross-origin redirect, a custom credential header
named in that discarded list can be forwarded to the redirect
destination. Patch25 (grafana-storybook-follow-redirects-cve.patch)
already bumped 1.16.0 -> 1.16.1, which is itself affected.

Generated against the post-Patch26 lockfile.
